team_fallback:
  current: actor_reviewed_and_lead_self_reviewed_for_chg_003_pending_merge_authorization
  reason: PR creation is still unavailable for this repository, so the previously authorized tool-unavailable integration fallback still applies; `CHG-003` is now reviewed and committed but not merged
  pr_attempt:
    command: gh pr create --base main --head codex/mutation-contract-test-slice
    result: failed
    error: "GraphQL: Resource not accessible by personal access token (createPullRequest)"
    note: gh is installed and authenticated as `fiq`, but the active personal access token lacks pull-request write scope; branch push succeeded
  actor_review: completed twice for `CHG-002`; completed once for the `CHG-003` `T8` fix on 2026-07-30, which returned a block-the-merge verdict
  chg_003_actor_review_outcome:
    - fixed: a command with no path separator was resolved against `PATH` rather than the candidate worktree when the target folder was the Git root, so something outside the candidate could satisfy a required behaviour; commands now always carry a `./` prefix
    - fixed: a missing or non-executable check script was reported as a failed behaviour case, indistinguishable from a candidate that broke the behaviour; the command now refuses to run
    - fixed: the one-check-per-declared-case invariant lived only in the CLI; `PhenotypeBridgeScorer` now fails the gate closed on a declared case with no evidence
    - fixed: `checkDirectory` had to be relative but nothing enforced it, so an absolute path would have escaped the candidate worktree
    - fixed: duplicate detection was case-sensitive, so on a case-insensitive filesystem `Foo` and `foo` would both exec `foo.sh` and count as two cases
    - fixed: pathspec anchoring depended on the caller's working directory; now anchored at the repository root with `:/` and `(top,exclude)`
    - fixed: stale `check.sh` references in `HANDOFF.toon` and the `CHG-003` design; the per-case timeout is now documented
    - recorded_not_fixed: reporters print only check name and status, so a failing behaviour case shows no diagnostics (task `T9`)
    - recorded_not_fixed: no gate requires a non-empty realization (task `T10`)
    - confirmed_not_a_defect: path traversal, leading-dash flag injection and check timeouts already failed closed, and the first-commit `<sha>^` case is unreachable because a candidate always commits on top of `HEAD`
  chg_003_second_actor_review: completed 2026-07-31 over only the fixes the lead had cleared itself; verdict do-not-merge
  chg_003_second_actor_review_outcome:
    - fixed: a tracked symlink out of the tree let a script that was not in the candidate satisfy a required behaviour and promote; containment is now enforced at execution against the candidate worktree
    - fixed: the bridge's evidence map was last-wins, so a passing check entry could overwrite a failing one for the same declared case and record the gate as satisfied
    - fixed: a blank declared behaviour case name crashed mid-scoring rather than failing the gate closed
    - fixed: two javadocs asserted containment guarantees the code did not provide
    - fixed: `forCases` guarded absolute check directories but not upward traversal
    - fixed: the blocker's regression test asserted the symptom rather than the property; an end-to-end symlink refusal test now covers it
    - recorded_not_fixed: the pre-flight validates the working tree while checks run against `HEAD` (task `T12`)
    - recorded_not_fixed: the POSIX-shaped convention and case-insensitive filesystem behaviour, recorded as `CHG-003` risks
    - adjusted_rather_than_applied: the suggested containment location would have broken the legitimate `sh -c` pattern, so containment covers only programs named by path
    - confirmed_not_a_defect: the pathspec change is byte-identical to the previous form from the repository root and strictly more robust from a subdirectory; `Set` iteration order is not observable in the recorded result; the pre-flight ordering is correct
  actor_review_outcome:
    - fixed: empty deterministic-check evidence no longer passes its hard gate
    - fixed: gate outcomes are recorded after measured scores so evidence cannot overwrite them in the audit record
    - fixed: canonicalizer rejects unsafe atoms and identifiers, closing IR node forgery and whitespace collisions
    - fixed: threshold comparison uses the raw score; rounding is reporting only
    - fixed: authority-language scan now covers search posture, parent traits, evidence and gate fields
    - fixed: conceptual crossover requires two distinct evaluated parents and validates its own child contract
    - recorded_not_fixed: declared contract hard gates are not enforced by the scorer (RISK-002, task T4b)
    - recorded_not_fixed: canonical IR is declaration-order sensitive for set-like fields (Q-007)
  lead_self_review: completed before each `CHG-002` merge; completed for `CHG-003` on 2026-07-30 after the actor findings were addressed
  chg_003_lead_self_review_outcome:
    - found: the `<name>.sh` convention was duplicated between `BehaviourCaseChecks` and the new fail-fast validation, so changing it in one place would drift; the validation now derives the script path from the emitted command
    - found: `seen.add` was a side effect inside a stream `map`; replaced with an explicit loop
    - no other findings; the diff adds no provider imports, no dead code and no silent TODOs, and `cli -> adapters` is a permitted direction
  restructure_review_outcome:
    - fixed: provider dependencies are now confined per package, closing the containment the adapter-module merge gave up
    - fixed: `settings.gradle.kts` no longer creates an empty `:modules` container project
    - fixed: stale `core/` and `application/` references in `docs/validation.md` and `docs/wiki/architecture.md`
    - fixed: `HANDOFF.toon` recorded the fitness function as unchanged in the same change that hardened it, and asserted a push that had not happened
    - fixed: `CHG-002` acceptance `test_id`s pointed at modules that no longer exist
    - fixed: deleted the consumed `CLAUDE_HANDOVER.toon` packet rather than maintaining its stale paths
  lost_challenge: no human code review; `CHG-002` and `CHG-003` reviews were agent actors. The first `CHG-003` review returned block-the-merge; its fixes were then re-reviewed independently, which found a surviving promotion-integrity hole, so the second review was load-bearing rather than confirmatory. The `T11` fixes answering that second review have themselves had only lead self-review, though they are covered by tests and verified against the real binary in fresh repositories. The user reported PR tooling is now available, so `CHG-003` goes through a pull request and human review rather than the PR-less fallback.
